                <pb facs="0173" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v06/pg138"/>

                <head>28. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Soviet Foreign Minister Andrei Gromyko
                    and Secretary of State Cyrus Vance met
                    May 18–20, 1977, in Geneva to discuss SALT II
                    and the Middle East. Four of the five meetings addressed SALT and especially how the United States and
                    Union of Soviet Socialist Republics could reach an agreement despite differing
                    goals and objectives following the Vladivostok negotiations. For a summary of
                    those meetings, see <ref target="frus:frus1969-76v33/d167">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1969–1976, volume XXXIII,
                            SALT II, 1972–1980, Document
                    167</ref>.</p>
            </div>
